WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.980
Congratulations!

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.730
You guys will be the regular team members!

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.820
Wait a minute manager...you're joking, right?

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.320
They haven't handled the ball and you've already decided based on the results of the run?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.950
Furthermore, why did you leave Murakoshi out?!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.210
I figured that you all won't be able to accept it, so for now I'll have you to accept it.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.330
Fifteen minutes from now...

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.210
I'll take command of this group.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.130
Coach, you'll command the other group.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.130
If you guys win, I'll reconsider my decision.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.050
In this way, no one should have any complaints, right?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.200
You guys becoming the substitutes...

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.910
I'm sure the manager didn't mean it.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.170
He's probably trying to rile you guys up.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.420
Right, Murakoshi?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.300
I don't know he's thinking,

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.670
But I only know that I have to win.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.520
We will win.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.440
But manager, the other side comprises of regulars...

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.650
Currently, you guys are just a bunch of substitutes.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.160
To put it short, you guys barely passed the pro level, a little better than the weaklings.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.660
Are you guys fine with that?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.870
Imagine.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.120
Defeating the regulars...

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.080
...and grabbing their spots.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.500
Then, go on to win league games.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.960
Your life will never be the same again.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.630
This is the first step towards your giant killing act!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.680
But it's not going to be an easy task...

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.850
Demoralised even before starting?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.940
Every match starts with a score of 0-0.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.940
This is fair towards everyone.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.940
But you guys will win.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.030
You have the ability to do so.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.450
Hey, Murakoshi and the rest are wearing yellow bibs.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.540
Isn't that what the substitutes usually wear?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.500
But Tatsumi's sitting on the bench over there...

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.130
Tatsumi...

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.470
What's the meaning of this, Tatsumi?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.180
Murakoshi shouldn't be a substitute, damn it!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.680
Defence style is man-marking.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.680
And Tsubaki's onto me...

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.980
I will not go easy on you!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.570
Reverse side!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.530
Hey!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.780
Going all out is good...

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.700
But today is the first day of practice!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.290
Put more thought into it!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.080
I'm sorry.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:40.000
No problem. Do the best that you can.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.550
Yes!

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.510
I thought he couldn't do anything right,

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.010
But he came at me at full force just now...

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.610
Fine. I accept the challenge.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.570
The ball's stolen!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.820
He's coming!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.160
Defend your zones properly!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.620
Are we going to chase after that?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.910
Never mind that, stop his passes!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.120
There's still a lot of open space!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.540
Both of you don't need to run forcefully after him!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.960
Once again, he's not passing it here!

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.090
Oh crap!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.100
Murakoshi, nice job!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:38.810
Why...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.400
Why are they not taking their chances?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.940
That team's composition...

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.610
...was based on those who did well in the thirty-meter dashes.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.160
They're a bunch of guys with fast legs.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.120
But why...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.330
Why aren't they using their speed to get hold of this match?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.170
Don't they have the guts?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.920
No, that's not it.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.430
This must be...

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.640
...part of his plan.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.020
That arrogant attitude of his hasn't change.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:17.980
I won't lose.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.770
You're the only person...

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.860
...that I cannot afford to lose to!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.280
Defence line! Pull your defences together!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.740
That was such a good chance...

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.160
They're pretty good, following my orders closely.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.580
With this kind of strategy, can we really win?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.630
Forbidding one-touch play...

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.960
Is that really okay?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.840
If one-touch play is allowed,

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.800
we might have scored a goal.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.430
It's fine.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.350
There's something more important than just scoring a goal.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.470
Showing it to them comes before that.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.020
And that will lead us to victory.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.730
We have to win no matter what.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.320
For ETU's sake.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.160
What's the matter with them?

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.240
How cowardly can they be?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:21.040
Thirty minutes have passed...and it's still goalless.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:26.880
Not only that, I feel like the game's already fallen to the pace of the other team.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.420
Hey, put more effort into covering up!

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:33.970
Yes.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.310
So that's how it is...

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:51.070
Listen carefully! From now on, stop trying to forcefully steal the ball away!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.660
They are just trying to make us run!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.540
Don't simply waste your energy! Just keep to your defence zone and it'll be fine!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.620
Dang, he figured it out.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.330
Guess I've got no choice.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.710
One-touch play ban is lifted!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.630
Go all out, you guys!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.180
Here comes a chance!

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.980
Nice clearance, Murakoshi!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.860
You idiot! Don't just dally around!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.190
Look at the ball closely!

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:30.820
I'm sorry.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.200
They pulled out such a beautiful pass out of a sudden...how?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.960
You're asking how? Well, that's because they're gathered together!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.340
You mean those guys who can run fast in the dashing exercise just now?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.050
There are many types of fast runners too!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:57.220
What I wanted was those who can still run fast even when exhausted.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.770
What I was looking at in the forty-five minutes dashing exercise was...

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.980
...the first and last minute.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.360
To put it more clearly, the time difference between these two minutes.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.650
The smaller the difference, the more stamina the person has.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.990
The faster the time, the more stamina and speed that the person has.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.210
And those are the guys in my team.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.670
Tatsumi's team.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:34.840
On the other hand, the opposing side are made to dash for the ball in a game of keep-away, wasting their energy.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.720
That was the purpose of forbidding one-touch play?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:44.310
Correct. With the guys on the other team tiring out, even our lousy passes will get through.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:50.360
So, what will do now, Mr ETU?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.490
Hey! Don't play into their tricks!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.740
Look at it properly!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.910
We're ETU's main weapons!

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.080
You don't call that a weapon, Murakoshi.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.840
Just defending all the way and doing counter attacks...

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.460
You’re saying that because you can no longer run.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.130
ETU's soccer is...

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.300
Hmm...

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:22.810
It's just not interesting, somehow.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.720
The shots on goal are few.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.060
It does have tense moments, but it doesn't make you leap in joy.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.150
Yes, that's the feeling!

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.820
Even the kids can already point out your weaknesses.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.070
This is an undeniable truth.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.160
Don't screw with me.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.660
As if I'm going to let things go your way.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.540
I have the technique and the experience.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:56.010
And more than that, I have the pride of getting ETU to the way it is now!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.800
Look forward! I'll show my comrades that I'll get through them!

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.180
As the captain...

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.280
My legs are giving away...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.370
Damn it!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.160
I...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.620
I still can...

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.750
Stop him!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.300
Murata!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.090
Keeper!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:40.050
Shoot it.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:52.900
Yes!!!

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.270
Nice shot!

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.360
You struck it well just now!

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.480
Awesome!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.190
Amazing!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.070
It really ended just like you said it would!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.450
It'll be a one-sided match from here onwards.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:08.660
I wonder who the weapon is now...

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:10.580
Murakoshi?

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.960
Or Tsubaki?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.110
Hey! Did you see that, Shige?

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.980
Tatsumi...

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.860
...is really doing his job!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.660
He's really back.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.280
ETU's ray of hope!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.870
It's been a long time since I felt like really cheering them on!

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.830
Same here!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.000
I still have their flag in my closet!

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.540
I've plumped up quite a bit so I can't wear their jersey!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.430
We really won!

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:10.760
Unbelievable!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.350
I actually scored two goals!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.690
Hey, tone it down!

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.080
Murakoshi...

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.370
East Tokyo United?

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.920
Why do you want to go to a team like that?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.840
Murakoshi, you could have aimed for better teams instead...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.840
I can be a regular immediately if I go there.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.130
Also...

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.680
ETU will get stronger from now onwards.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:01.690
If we combined our strength, it's no longer just a dream to be a big club.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.910
It's the rookie, Murakoshi!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.160
Yeah! We might be able to clinch the cup again!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.120
Good job, Murakoshi!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.120
Next time, come to my shop!

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.210
I'll let you eat for free!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.420
Murakoshi, don't go! Their food is bad!

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.880
What did you say?!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.010
Come to our Chinese restaurant instead!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.760
I'll treat you to pan-fried dumplings!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.720
I've always believed in becoming stronger...

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.310
...just like that time.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.650
Can you give us your autograph please?

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.990
But...why?!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.090
Can I ask a question?

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.970
Please! Please do ask!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.010
Yesterday, you had your boys play in a match even though you're just appointed,

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.050
between the regulars and the substitutes,

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.810
which ended in a one-sided victory for the subs.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.940
And you're the one who was in charge of the subs.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.940
Would that mean that you're planning to change the players?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:27.730
I wonder about that.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.610
Say it out clearly!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.200
Then, along with my impression of the situation, allow me to ask you directly.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.500
Is there a possibility that even Mr ETU, Murakoshi...

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.920
...will be relegated to the reserves?

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.130
I don't know.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.300
But...

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.730
I can only tell you this.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.650
Regarding the player, Murakoshi...

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:06.770
Koshi!

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.070
That guy, just now at the media conference-

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.070
Damn, it's tiring!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.530
But well, it's a big success!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.450
Tatsumi! Saying that out just now,

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.170
didn't you even consider about Murakoshi's feelings?

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.750
That's a little too harsh on him!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.710
Wait!

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.060
Just at the right time.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.150
What do you plan to do?

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.110
Coming back suddenly...

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.690
...and messing up the team big time!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:56.160
Above all, you're removing me as the captain?!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.950
What do you know about ETU?

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:05.170
I fought alongside ETU for ten years!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.500
The one who abandoned ETU...

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.500
What do you know about it?

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.760
The first impression's important.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:17.050
I can see the team's weakness clearly precisely because I'm not familiar with it.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:20.010
Sometimes, there's also a need to leave it to someone else to handle things.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.720
Are you saying that my presence...

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.850
...is the reason for the team's weakness?

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.190
No need of players who can no longer run?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:33.690
A captain who was completely defeated by a bunch of greenhorns?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.700
That's the one thing I don't want to hear from you!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.120
ETU crumbled after you left!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.450
Even when we're relegated and not sponsored, I stayed!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.920
Because I felt it was my responsibility as the captain!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.250
Pulling together a team from a bunch of depressed guys...

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.460
We managed to get ourselves back to the first division after four years!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.470
I had given my all in rebuilding the team that you destroyed!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.760
A loss again!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.970
How many years are we going to stay in the second division?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.890
Didn't it go downhill after Tatsumi left?

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.730
They're right...

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.030
We've fallen that much...

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.160
Manager!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.120
When will Jorgino play again?

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.120
That guy returned back to Brazil already.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.790
Damn it, using useless foreigners who can't even play...

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.300
Can we even win with that front?

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:40.840
Come with me.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.720
We can't count on help from others.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:50.310
If we listen to what the higher-ups says, we won't be able to win.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.520
We are going to grab it with our own strength.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.610
For that, I will...

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.700
...bet everything I have!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:10.170
The team's offensive power, balance; I've searched for whatever methods that we can use to win.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:14.880
I've sacrificed everything to get this team to the top.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.050
Can you, who only think for yourself...

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.970
...even understand my feelings?

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.970
I've done everything a captain has to do.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:28.810
For the past ten years, I've bet everything I had on ETU!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:35.190
That's why I'm relieving you of your captain duties.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.530
The team's situation...

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.150
The team's balance...

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:42.450
Offensive power...

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.490
There is no need for you to worry about them.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:52.460
To put it short, you were just not blessed with a good coach.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.550
You lost in the match just now.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.510
You can't run as fast as the youngsters.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:06.140
Even so, find the weapon that will enable you to win.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.270
In exchange,

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.400
The burden you have carried on your shoulders for all this while...

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.900
...let me bear half of it, with my life on the line!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.250
It's cold...

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:39.590
The other teams are all in the South training comfortably...

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.800
It can't be helped. We're a poor club afterall.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.680
Cold! Are we really going to train here?

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.480
Isn't that your suggestion in the first place?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.230
Even I didn't want it! I'd rather go for somewhere in the South!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.610
You're just all words, aren't you?

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:05.030
Seeing you from the time when you were playing actively as an ace,

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.830
Aren't you basking in the limelight as a manager too?

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:14.830
Being fine even when seeing the guys below you suffering; you seem to be just such a person.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.250
Hey Kuroda! Cut it out!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:20.880
I'm sorry, manager.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.380
I am not really bothered about it.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:24.970
Those two...

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.220
Kuroda and Sugie...how should I say it?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:33.600
They are Murakoshi's loyal followers.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:37.770
It's probably because you stripped Murakoshi of his captaincy.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.110
As I thought, that's going to be the issue that has to be ironed out first.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:49.910
And now,

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:54.620
I'll announce the content for the first day of the yearly ETU training camp.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.330
Self-practice!

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.050
Umm...

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:06.800
What?

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.430
Self-practice! Don't you know about it?

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:11.890
Self-practice!

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:14.470
No, that's not what I meant...

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:19.020
Like I said, think about what you need to do on your own.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.610
You don't just listen to what the manager says.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:26.150
But have initiative to do what you need to do, that's how a pro does it.

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:31.070
And so, since it's so cold, I'll go warm myself up a little.

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:36.330
Come on, put some effort in it now!

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.250
By the way Murakoshi,

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:44.630
You're no longer the captain...

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:48.590
...so don't go around ordering people, okay?

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:16.970
Where did that idiot of a manager go?

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:18.600
To hell with self-practice!

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:19.680
Do you think you can win?

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:22.890
This looks bad, manager!

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.850
I was just thinking of making it a little more interesting.

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:25.980
Luigi Yoshida.

00:24:26.690 --> 00:24:28.270
People call me Gino.
